# Versioning & Changelog

- Use [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/): MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH
- Version lives in `mrc-exporter.toc` (`## Version`) and should stay in sync with `Addon.version` in `mrc-exporter.lua`
- When releasing: bump both version locations, then add a `CHANGELOG.md` entry
- Changelog entries must describe **actual user-facing changes** included in the release (from commits/diff since the previous release), not just “bump version”

## Changelog format

- Follow [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/)
- File: `CHANGELOG.md` at project root
- Sections: `### Added`, `### Changed`, `### Deprecated`, `### Removed`, `### Fixed`, `### Security`
- Entry format: `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD`
- Add new entries at the top (above previous releases)
- Do **not** add filler entries like “version bump for release”; if a release has no notable changes, do not cut a release (or explicitly document why)

## Version bump rules

- **PATCH** — bug fixes, minor tweaks
- **MINOR** — new features, non-breaking changes
- **MAJOR** — breaking changes (use `BREAKING CHANGE` in commit)
